# The log of the test must have a line for each of these patterns (grep -E).
# The pistol comes with a full clip of 6 rounds, and the HUD shows them.
\[5\.00\].* inv count=3 WeaponPistol Ammo10mm NanoKeyRing
\[7\.00\].* text x=74 y=429 "6"
\[7\.10\].* dump Terrorist3 .* health=75 
# The first shot starts the fight, and the music goes to the combat section, which is order 3.
Music: LibertyIsland_Music section 3 starts at order 3
# Three shots take three rounds. The guard has damage or is dead.
\[11\.00\].* text x=74 y=429 "3"
!\[11\.10\].* dump Terrorist3 .* health=75 
# After six shots the clip is empty and the guard is dead: the list of all guards has no line for it.
\[15\.00\].* text x=74 y=429 "0"
!\[15\.10\].* dump Terrorist3 
# The map has the body TerroristCarcass0, so the body of the guard gets the next number. It has the pistol of the guard.
\[15\.20\].* dump TerroristCarcass1 state=Dead .* Inventory=WeaponPistol'WeaponPistol[0-9]+'
\[15\.30\].* dump Ammo10mm[0-9]+ .* AmmoAmount=0 Owner=JCDentonMale'JCDentonMale0'
# The search gives the knife of the guard, and the rounds of its pistol go to the player.
\[17\.00\].* inv count=5 WeaponCombatKnife AmmoNone WeaponPistol Ammo10mm NanoKeyRing
\[17\.20\].* dump TerroristCarcass1 .* Inventory=None
\[17\.30\].* dump Ammo10mm[0-9]+ .* AmmoAmount=[1-9][0-9]* Owner=JCDentonMale'JCDentonMale0'
!Accessed None
